ber one in New Zealand, and was certified Gold in its first week. The album was certified Platinum in its second week, selling over 15,000 copies. In September 2011, Home Improvement Retailer Lowe's began a new brand campaign featuring Wigmore's single \\\"Don't Stop\\\". \\\"Holy Smoke\\\" debuted at\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01\", \"text\": \"Holy Smoke (Peter Murphy album) Holy Smoke is the fourth solo studio album by English musician Peter Murphy. It was released on 14 April 1992 through Beggars Banquet Records. Produced by Mike Thorne, the album features contributions from Alison Limerick, Jonathan Carney, Audrey Riley and The Hundred Men, his backing band since 1988's \\\"Love Hysteria\\\" album. Although the album didn't meet with the commercial success of its predecessor, \\\"Deep\\\" (1990), it peaked at number 108 on \\\"Billboard\\\" 200 chart. The lead single off the album, \\\"The Sweetest Drop\\\", peaked at number 2 on Billboard Modern Rock Tracks chart. Ned Raggett\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [], \"prior_explanation\": \"I am uncertain about an album titled 'Holy Smoke'. The phrase is famously associated with the band Scorpions' song, but no major album by that exact title exists in my knowledge.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Gin Wigmore\", \"scope\": \"Artist of the album Holy Smoke\", \"claim\": \"Holy Smoke is the debut album from New Zealand pop singer Gin Wigmore.\", \"answer\": \"Gin Wigmore\", \"quote\": \"Holy Smoke (Gin Wigmore album) Holy Smoke is the debut album from New Zealand pop singer Gin Wigmore, released under the mononym Gin.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Peter Murphy\", \"scope\": \"Artist of the album Holy Smoke\", \"claim\": \"Holy Smoke is the fourth solo studio album by English musician 